## TLS

An HTTPS relationship between two nodes in the cluster is TLS. cert-manager issues a self-signed CA in the namespace
and, from it, a certificate for each destination's Service name (`tls.yaml`). The destination runs an nginx sidecar
(`tls-proxy`) that serves it on {{tls.containerPort}} (Service port {{tls.servicePort}}) and forwards to its container over
localhost; the network policies allow {{tls.containerPort}}, not the plain port. The source mounts the CA certificate at
`{{tls.caDir}}/ca.crt`{{#if gatewayTls}}, and the gateway checks the service's certificate with it{{/if}}. The cluster needs
cert-manager (`yarn k8s:up` installs it).

| Node | Certificate secret |
|---|---|
{{#each tlsWorkloads}}
| `{{id}}` | `{{tls.secretName}}` |
{{/each}}

During an upgrade from 1.2.1, traffic through the gateway can fail until the gateway pod has rolled out and the
certificate is issued. nginx does not reload when cert-manager renews the CA or a certificate: restart the pods after
a renewal.
{{/if}}

